<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Kitāb al-mukhtaṣar fī ḥisāb al-jabr wal-muqābala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">820 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as al-Kitāb al-mukhtaṣar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kitob">Kitab</a> al-mukhtasar fi hisab al-jabr wal-muqabala, the Compendious Book on Calculation by Completion and Balancing, is a mathematical treatise by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-khwarizmi">al-Khwarizmi</a> written in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> around 820 CE. It set out systematic methods for solving linear and quadratic equations, and the word <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algebra">algebra</a> derives from al-jabr in its title. It is one of the best-known scientific achievements of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-kitab-al-mukhtasar-fi-hisab-al-jabr-wal-muqabala.jpg" alt="Al-Kitāb al-mukhtaṣar fī ḥisāb al-jabr wal-muqābala" width="240" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Muḥammad ibn Musa al-Khwarizmi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Image-Al-Kit%C4%81b_al-mu%E1%B8%ABta%E1%B9%A3ar_f%C4%AB_%E1%B8%A5is%C4%81b_al-%C4%9Fabr_wa-l-muq%C4%81bala.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
